      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684557631">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP394 Aldergrove School&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My second cap of the day and another one that took me a few minutes.  I am grateful to the few cap crazies who have come before me and have dug these caps out recently and those who provided great context pictures.  This saved me a few times this past week and allowed me a fun finding experience.  Eventually I spotted this one too.  Took my pics and was on my way to the next one.  :)  TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682470593">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP394 Aldergrove School

While in the west end decided to grab a couple more BCPs. Was starting to drizzle a bit but wasn't going to let that deter us. 

The cap was pretty easy to find using the Context photos and the fairly obvious divot. That said it was already starting to grow in so we had to trowel out some dirt and grass roots then clean off the cap to read the numbers. Took some pics then hurried back to the car before getting too wet.

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680191946">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3854161">Stonagal</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP394 - Aldergrove School

Took a few minutes, but eventually the context photos got me where I needed to go. Made out a few digits. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="659594464">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7338377">j0ckser</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP394-Aldergrove School

&lt;strong&gt;GPSr reads N 53° 31.138 W 113° 38.015&lt;/strong&gt;

Cap in passable condition. Most numbers readable.

Email with info sent.

GeoGuider and I were making the most of the Canada Day long weekend.  We picked up several BCPs, including this one. TFTC OFTH.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="614180277">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1095439">GeoGuider</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP394 Aldergrove School&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Posted:  N53° 31.138     W113° 38.016&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;My GPSr:  N53° 31.138     W113° 38.016&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we were going to be in the West End for WillowZilla's Game Night to celebrate Canada Day anyway, j0ckser and I thought we'd go look up this brass cap before we got there.  We found it in fairly short order, but had to clean it off quite a bit before we could take pictures.  We had j0ckser's new metal detector with us, but didn't need it.  Some Canada Day celebrants walked by asking if we'd found any gold yet.  &quot;Nope, just brass!&quot;  Thanks for the BCP, OFTH. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
